<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gonzalo Pizarro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510–<a href="/years/1548">1548</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonzalo Pizarro was a Spanish conquistador and younger half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a>. He took part in the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a> and led an expedition to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> in 1541. In 1544 he led the encomenderos' revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws</a>, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blasco-nunez-vela">Blasco Núñez Vela</a> in 1546, but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-la-gasca">Pedro de la Gasca</a> at Jaquijahuana in 1548 and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gonzalo-pizarro.jpg" alt="Gonzalo Pizarro" width="240" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gonzalo_Pizarro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
